ly  travel across the border and make a  profit of 50 in three months he didn't  have any money of his own so he gave his  friends an opportunity to finance this  venture  one of them agreed to invest 200 in the  company  and this is how the securities exchange  company appeared  news about the financial startup spread  all over the city and soon the company  was attracting 250 000 a day  however this story came to an end as  early as 1920. kwanzi's friend the one  who made the initial investment demanded  50 of the company's current income  through the court  now he lost the lawsuit but the ministry  of finance became interested in the huge  revenues this company was generating it  soon became clear that the way the ponzi  scheme worked was completely differently  to how it had been described ponzi  didn't buy any coupons in fact this  story was invented solely for  authenticity's sake  in fact the ponzi scheme paid dividends  to the old participants at the expense  of the new ones  a beautiful legend aggressive  advertising and a constant influx of new  users who dream of a return on their  investments  does it remind you of anything  now i'm sure none of you have missed the  news about bitcoin's dramatic fall from  grace  crucially the flagship cryptocurrency is  now dragging the entire crypto market  down to the bottom remember i mentioned  the board ape yacht club project  recently  the man who changed the modern world  made reference to it on techcrunch  bill gates the founder of microsoft and  one of the richest people in the world  used this nft as an example i don't know  i mean obviously expensive you know  digital images of monkeys are going to  improve the world immensely uh we all  agree on it and uh you know that's so  incredible now gates attributed the  success of the nft market as a whole to  the theory of the bigger fool  when the buyer of an overpriced asset  expects to sell it to someone who will  give even more now i wonder he'll be  right the creative windows or the  industry with a turnover of 22 billion  anyway we'll find out soon enough but  thanks for tuning in today guys this was  emily with some sub and i'll be waiting  for you on our next tour of the online  jungle  [Music]  you
 

